\label{sec:main_results}

RR-MoA's case rests on three claims: fixed-topology adapters are suboptimal, the natural MoE remedy collapses on instance-normalized backbones, and the collapse cannot be recovered by standard rescue mechanisms. We establish each in turn before comparing against the seven-baseline suite (fixed adapters, LoRA, TRACE, independent ensembles, AdaMix, full fine-tuning, DLinear).

